# Frame and overlays: an Overlay is placed with Offset against the Frame that contains it, at a corner, along a side or stretched.
Document (dev.stxt.pdf):
	Language: en
	Title: Frame and overlays · Overlay and Offset
	Page:
		Paper: A4
		Margin: 20mm
	Section:
		Text: Frame and overlays
			Style: topic
		Heading 1:
			Text: Overlay and Offset
		Paragraph: An `Overlay` leaves the flow and takes no space. Each side of its `Offset` is the distance to that edge of the nearest `Frame` (or the page area), and `auto` leaves the side free. With both sides of an axis set, the box stretches between them.
			Style: intro
		Text: The four corners and the center of the left side
			Style: label
		Frame:
			Style: stage
			Overlay:
				Offset: 10 auto auto 10
				Text: 10 auto auto 10
					Style: badge
			Overlay:
				Offset: 10 10 auto auto
				Text: 10 10 auto auto
					Style: badge
			Overlay:
				Offset: auto auto 10 10
				Text: auto auto 10 10
					Style: badge
			Overlay:
				Offset: auto 10 10 auto
				Text: auto 10 10 auto
					Style: badge
			Overlay:
				Offset: 50% auto auto 10
				Text: 50% auto auto 10  (the top at half the height)
					Style: badge
		Text: Stretched between two sides
			Style: label
